      "sourceHash": "5eb3e8dae7751a1a085be1699650f2bf0d740de6947a80b573030a671d76ced4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.91,
          "end": 5.44,
          "en": "So sending requests to store data is one thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.45,
          "end": 8.33,
          "en": "Now, I also want to fetch my data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.42,
          "end": 11.96,
          "en": "And of course, I want to do that when my app loads here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.59,
          "end": 16.28,
          "en": "Now, what would be the right place to then send such a request?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.61,
          "end": 22.52,
          "en": "Well, we can do it just here, right in the script tags, not inside of some function, but just here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 22.52,
          "end": 25.28,
          "en": "When this code gets executed, when this app loads.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 25.28,
          "end": 31.04,
          "en": "Because you learned in the component section that this script tag always gets executed when this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 31.04,
          "end": 33.32,
          "en": "is added to the Dom when it is loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 33.5,
          "end": 36.05,
          "en": "So here again we can send a fetch request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.08,
          "end": 40.47,
          "en": "The URL, of course is the same because that is the place where we store our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.49,
          "end": 46.13,
          "en": "Now it is a get request, so we don't need to set up this second configuration object because we're",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 46.13,
          "end": 51.53,
          "en": "also not adding any body, we're not sending any data and therefore we also don't need to define the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 51.53,
          "end": 54.43,
          "en": "content type of any data because there isn't any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.44,
          "end": 58.64,
          "en": "And instead we can just add then and catch right away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 59.43,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "So here and then we get a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 68.43,
          "en": "And just as before, I want to check if that is okay and throw an error if it is not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 74.46000000000001,
          "en": "And here we do get our error and I simply want to log it here so that we see what is wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 74.46000000000001,
          "end": 78.93,
          "en": "But if we make it past this here, then I want to work with that response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 79.16,
          "end": 84.45,
          "en": "Now, here, it's important to understand that response actually is a response object where the body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 84.45,
          "end": 85.44,
          "en": "of the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 85.44,
          "end": 91.02,
          "en": "So the data that was actually fetched has not been unpacked or converted yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 91.05,
          "end": 93.36,
          "en": "It's not readable yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 93.39,
          "end": 101.91,
          "en": "Instead, here we have to call response Json to convert the body of the incoming response back to normal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 101.91,
          "end": 102.81,
          "en": "JavaScript data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 102.81,
          "end": 105.66,
          "en": "So to convert it from Json to JavaScript data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 105.75,
          "end": 107.97,
          "en": "And that actually also yields a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 107.97,
          "end": 113.58,
          "en": "So if I just return it here, we simply make it into the next then block, which we can chain here and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 113.58,
          "end": 113.97,
          "en": "there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 113.97,
          "end": 115.2,
          "en": "We now get our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 115.2,
          "end": 119.77000000000001,
          "en": "That was part of the response and we can now use that data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 119.86,
          "end": 125.56,
          "en": "Now for a start, let's simply log data so that we can get a feeling for what we're fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 125.56,
          "end": 127.87,
          "en": "And as this reloads, this is what we get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 127.9,
          "end": 132.48,
          "en": "We get a JavaScript object in this case with two key value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 132.49,
          "end": 138.67000000000002,
          "en": "The keys are these unique, automatically generated IDs which Firebase gives us, and the values are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 138.67000000000002,
          "end": 139.99,
          "en": "the values we stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 140.26,
          "end": 143.02,
          "en": "Now we actually need an array here, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 143.02,
          "end": 145.48,
          "en": "Because hobbies here actually is an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 145.63,
          "end": 153.43,
          "en": "So since we need an array, we need to transform this object to an array that's relatively easy to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 153.43,
          "end": 157.57,
          "en": "If you need the IDs, you can use a for in loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 157.57,
          "end": 164.62,
          "en": "If you just need the values and you you are fine with dropping the key names, you can simply say hobbies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 164.65,
          "end": 172.39,
          "en": "is equal to object dot values data and this will just extract the values in that array or in that object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 172.39,
          "end": 174.01,
          "en": "and therefore you get that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 174.01,
          "end": 181.39,
          "en": "Now, if you need it, the keys, then you could get the those two with keys with the help of object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 181.39,
          "end": 183.16,
          "en": "keys data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 183.66,
          "end": 185.48,
          "en": "We can console log this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 191.73,
          "en": "Or if you have a more complex transformation, you can use a for in loop and for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 192.77,
          "end": 194.75,
          "en": "The key in data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 195.75,
          "end": 201.81,
          "en": "You can then also do something with that and you can console.log the key and also.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 203.11,
          "end": 206.74,
          "en": "The value for that key with this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 206.74,
          "end": 208.09,
          "en": "So that's another option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 208.09,
          "end": 212.26,
          "en": "If you plan on doing more complex transformations with that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 212.71,
          "end": 216.25,
          "en": "And I should of course define keys here as a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 217.79,
          "end": 219.71,
          "en": "So now you see some output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 219.74,
          "end": 221.81,
          "en": "These are my keys which are locked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 221.84,
          "end": 223.02,
          "en": "Keys not defined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 223.04,
          "end": 227.78,
          "en": "Yes, because here we should also add a const in front of that or a let.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 228.07999999999998,
          "end": 229.73,
          "en": "And now this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 229.76,
          "end": 233.03,
          "en": "So now these are the different ways of extracting the data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 233.03,
          "end": 235.25,
          "en": "We only need that to extract the values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 235.25,
          "end": 240.17,
          "en": "But of course it's quite common and we'll need it later in the course project that you also are interested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 240.17,
          "end": 243.83,
          "en": "in these unique IDs which Firebase gives you, and that is how you can get them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 243.83,
          "end": 249.8,
          "en": "Or you use this complete foreign loop here to have full control over what you're extracting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
